    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting the favorable matchups against Alcantara and Rodriguez. **Kyle Tucker** (74.54) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.37) headline our lineup as the strongest plays, both benefiting from a soft matchup against Alcantara (4.41 xERA). **Kyle Tucker** remains our most consistent offensive engine, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sees a significant boost from a dynamic platoon advantage that outweighs his historical BvP struggles. **Andy Pages** (70.52) also serves as a pillar for our production today, utilizing a 13% SP skill edge to capitalize on what should be a productive afternoon against Rodriguez.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today centered on the bottom of the order, specifically evaluating the marginal utility of **Nasim Nunez** (57.06) against the rest of our depth. While **Nasim Nunez** carries a lower projection due to his #9 spot in the order, his speed profile is vital to our stolen base strategy, keeping him ahead of alternatives like **Coby Mayo** or **Brayan Rocchio** who lack the same base-stealing upside. **Josh Jung** (56.59) sits on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier; his lack of a platoon advantage keeps him firmly in the \"Marginal\" category, though he remains a reliable start given the lack of superior options. Meanwhile, the optimizer continues to signal caution regarding **Miguel Vargas** (42.28) and **Sam Antonacci** (45.07) as they face a formidable arm in Ryan (3.21 xERA). \n\nWe are navigating several roster limitations, most notably the inactivity of our core stars **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill**, who are all sidelined by team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining on the IL, our daily efficiency relies heavily on the aforementioned platoon matchups to maintain our 5x5 standing. We will continue to monitor the lineup status for **Liam Hicks** (52.96) as his #1 spot provides high volatility, though his current score remains stable enough to warrant a start despite Cavalli\u2019s decent 3.74 xERA.",
